Z||000000||Formula_For_Sale||04-07-2001||08:52 PM|||| What can i do to get more horsepower to a 88 formula(all stock)? thinking about a computer chip but is there something else that works better? If you will tell me what gave you the most horsepower besides a new engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||3
Z||000001||Will||04-07-2001||10:15 PM||||A 250 shot of Nitrous--<P>Oops, sorry. That falls under new engine.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||04-07-2001||10:48 PM||||To get noticable horsepower increase it takes $$.  For the money you would need to spend to get more HP out of a stock 2.8 you could get a new engine.  A chip doesn't do that much.  A good tune up, wires,plugs, coil, distributor,sensor check/replacement, clean the thottle body, port polish intake and exhaust (headers), free flowing exhaust is all that is needed.||||reg||3
Z||000003||88formula||04-07-2001||11:26 PM||||1, Headers $800 coated and 20 horsepower with performance exhaust system. <BR>2, Aluminum flywheel $475 and a faster revving engine that gets more of the engines horsepower to the rear wheels.<BR>3, Camshaft and lifters $160 and 15 more horsepower.<BR>4, Crane Gold Race roller rocker arms $320 and five more horsepower with a cool sound.<BR>5, blended intake and exhaust bowls in heads with valve job $600 and 8-10 more horsepower<BR>6, 50-shot of nitrous somewhere around $500 and 40-50 more horsepower with a sh_t load more torque.<BR>7, underdrive pulley $80 and a claimed 6% more horsepower to the rear wheels.<BR>8, SI stainless steel valves and probably 5 or more horsepower $130.<BR>9, Borla exhaust system $400-$500 and 7 more horsepower.<BR>10, Crane multiple spark discharge ignition system with probably 2-4 more horsepower.<BR>11, K&N air filter $30 with probably a 1-2 horsepower increase.<BR>12, Cloyes double roller timing chain $90 with probably a 1 horsepower increase.<BR>13, Design one turbocharger system $3000-$4000 with a 60-85 horsepower increase.<BR>14, Ported exhaust manifolds $50 and 8 more horsepower.<P><BR>Best bang for your buck is porting your own exhaust manifolds. <P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||86GT Turbo||04-07-2001||11:37 PM||||I run a old miller-woods turbo in my GT<BR>at 11 psig boost I also run water injection with cam and ported heads,SI valves,3.1 injectors and a hi flo fuel pump plus some other stuff<BR>and I'm turning 13.4 in the Quarter<BR>the best bet is to find a old miller-woods turbo but make sure its a complete kit<BR>ie. chip and exhaust.||||reg||6
Z||000005||Formula_For_Sale||04-07-2001||11:43 PM||||thanx alot 88 formula very informative, if i did some of that stuff do you think it would take away from the cars price? b/c it's not all original then. i think i might need a new exhaust b/c the car sat in a garage for 11 year and the air filter broke up and i think some may have got stuck, but i'm not sure. Just asking b/c i raced a new dodge v8 mag. and when go to 100 i was only little over a care link, and a sunfire i raced was head to head forawhile until i won of course <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Formula_For_Sale||04-07-2001||11:46 PM||||where would i find a miller woods turbo kit?<BR>i mean do they still make them or should i post a new topic for one ?||||reg||1
Z||000007||Formula88||04-08-2001||12:18 AM||||Well, you could port your own exhaust manifolds.  That's free and supposed to give up to 10 hp.  You could add 1.6 ratio rocker arms for a bit more lift at the valves.  I'd put in a free flow air intake, just for the sound if nothing else.  I'm still looking for ideas for my '88 Formula.  I want it to look stock, but be as strong as possible.  When/if I replace my 2.8, I'm going with a 3.4 with hopefully around 200-250 HP, depending on what's available.  I want to keep everything LOOKING stock, though.  You could try the headers from West Coast Fiero.  I'd forget the chip.  All it'll do is tune the car to run with a 160 thermo, and thats not really needed.  I'd just go with Rodney's 180 thermo and low temp fan switch.  Not a horsepower gain, per se, but it'll help you get the most from other mods.  A free flow cat and exhaust will help a lot, too.||||reg||4
Z||000008||Eric||04-08-2001||12:21 AM||||Ported exhaust manifolds are the way to go.  It's free to do, if you have the tools, and it's dyno proven to make more horsepower.  You could try a K&N too.  It'll be good for about 1-2 horsepower, but it's only $25 or so.  So you're looking at 10 horsepower for very little money and just a little time (that forward manifold can be tricky to get off. Kroil and time works best).<P>A turbo will cost $2000 minimum to do correctly, but $4000 is more realistic.  Nitrous is the best bang for the buck power adder there is.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Predator||04-08-2001||07:18 AM||||If you want to check out the Turbo kit go to <A HREF="http://www.design1systems.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.design1systems.com</A>  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Sillhouette.com||04-08-2001||08:54 AM||||You could try a supercharger kit.  Vortech G90 bolt on designed for the STOCK engines but if you have mods done to it like exhaust heads and intake so much the better.  The Rotrax that was the unit before the Vortech gave 80HP and 100Tq.  This would give more because it runs at the 10psi level.  This pressure is very conservative as I said designed for stock.  some stronger bottom end and low pressure pistons and you can easily increase the psi to a MAX 20.  One catch no AC but that was not the title of your post.  More horespower you can't beat the SC. <P>here is the link.   <A HREF="http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://webhome.idirect.com/~rsm1/fiero_catalog.htm</A> <P>Later<BR>||||reg||1
